{
  "id": "helplessness-theory",
  "term": "helplessness theory",
  "definition": "Helplessness theory, as used here in learned helplessness theory, explains motivational withdrawal as developing when people come to expect that their efforts will not make a difference. In this view, anticipated failure and a sense that effort is ineffective can lead to disengagement rather than simple unwillingness.",
